        "workflow": {
          "name": "archon-merge-queue",
          "description": "The merge queue: merges the pull requests the build queue finished, and stops only\nfor decisions that belong to a person. Each run claims every waiting item with\nintake's claim, up to limit. One sweep agent decides each pull request and merges\nwhat policy allows, one at a time, through a gate script that refuses unless the\ntrusted review verdict says Ready at the head, CI is green there, the head contains\nthe default branch or merges into it cleanly, and the default branch's CI is not\nred, and merges pinned to that head. The queue never pushes and never waits for CI:\na conflict, a stale verdict or red the change caused goes back to the build queue,\nand the default branch's CI after a merge is the next sweep's first fact. A clear\ncase acts on its own; anything unclear pauses as one attention item whose answer is\na declared choice.\n\nUse when: a trigger binding the operator installed starts it (see the SDLC pack\nREADME, \"Merge queue\").\nNOT for: delivering or fixing a pull request (archon-build-queue, archon-ship), or\nreviewing one by hand (archon-review).\n",
